.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt MAKE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm make
.Nd maintain targets from makefile rules
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -posix
.Op Fl ehiknpqrSst
.Op Fl C Ar dir
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl j Ar num_jobs
.Op Fl x Ar pragma
.Op Ar macro Ns Li "[:[:[:]]]=\&" Ns Ar value ...
.Op Ar target ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
creates or updates files according to rules in makefiles.
Each file to be updated is a target.
A rule gives its prerequisites and the commands needed to build it.
Prerequisites may themselves be targets and are built first.
Rules may be explicit or inferred.
.Pp
Rach2 installs pdpmake 2.0.4 as the static i386 executable
.Pa /bin/make .
The built-in macros are
.Ql CC=tcc
and
.Ql LDFLAGS=-static
in extension, POSIX.1-2024 and POSIX.1-2017 modes.
The image has
.Nm tcc
and
.Nm cc ,
but no
.Nm c99
or
.Nm c17 .
Every program must be linked statically.
.Pp
The staged kernel, utility and ISH sources are under
.Pa /src/rach2 ,
.Pa /src/utils
and
.Pa /src/ish .
Each has a
.Pa guest.mk
written for pdpmake.
.Ss Input files
Without
.Fl f ,
.Nm
searches the working directory for
.Pa PDPmakefile ,
which strict POSIX mode selected before the input is read skips,
.Pa makefile
and
.Pa Makefile ,
in that order, and uses the first one found.
The filename
.Ql -
means standard input.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -posix
Enable strict POSIX mode.
This must be the first command-line option.
.It Fl C Ar dir
Change to
.Ar dir ;
strict POSIX mode rejects the option.
before execution.
Repeated options are relative to the preceding directory;
.Ql -C / -C etc
is equivalent to
.Ql -C /etc .
.It Fl e
Let environment variables override the makefile's macro assignments;
command-line assignments still take precedence.
.It Fl f Ar file
Read the makefile
.Ar file .
Repeated options read the files in the order given.
.It Fl h
Print help; strict POSIX mode rejects the option.
.It Fl i
Ignore unsuccessful command exits and continue.
This is equivalent to the special target
.Ql .IGNORE
without prerequisites.
.It Fl j Ar num_jobs
Ignored.
Accepted for compatibility with other make implementations; POSIX.1-2017
mode rejects it.
Recipes run serially.
.It Fl k
Continue processing after an error.
Do not execute recipes for targets that depend on failed targets.
.It Fl n
Print commands without executing them, except commands prefixed with
.Ql +
or expanding
.Va MAKE ,
and the recipes that rebuild included makefiles, which still run.
.It Fl p
Print macro definitions and rules during execution.
.It Fl q
Execute no rules, except commands prefixed with
.Ql + .
Exit successfully if the requested targets are up to date, or with status 1
otherwise.
.It Fl r
Do not use built-in rules; clear the suffix list.
.It Fl S
Stop after an error.
This is the default and reverses
.Fl k .
.It Fl s
Do not print commands as they execute.
This is equivalent to the special target
.Ql .SILENT
without prerequisites.
.It Fl t
Touch target files instead of executing rules, except commands prefixed
with
.Ql + ,
which run.
Ignore targets that are up to date or have no rules.
.It Fl x Ar pragma
Enable an extension in strict POSIX mode.
May be repeated.
The pragmas are listed below.
.It Ar macro Ns Li "[:[:[:]]]=\&" Ns Ar value
Assign
.Ar value
to
.Ar macro ,
overriding its definition in the input.
Assignments and targets may be mixed on the command line, as an
extension; strict POSIX mode requires the assignments first.
Assignments are processed first.
.El
.Ss Pragmas
Pragmas selectively enable extensions in strict POSIX mode.
.Bl -tag -width command_comment
.It Ql macro_name
Allow
.Ql -
in macro names.
.It Ql target_name
Allow
.Ql -
and
.Ql /
in target names.
.It Ql command_comment
Do not treat
.Ql #
as a comment introducer in commands or target and inference rules.
.It Ql empty_suffix
Allow an empty suffix in macro expansions, as in
.Ql $(VAR:=.c) .
.It Ql posix_2017
Enforce POSIX.1-2017.
.It Ql posix_2024
Enforce POSIX.1-2024.
This standard permits the characters enabled by
.Ql macro_name
and
.Ql target_name
without those pragmas.
.It Ql posix_202x
An alias for
.Ql posix_2024 .
.It Ql windows
Allow Windows paths as target names.
This may also require
.Ql target_name .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /src/rach2/guest.mk
.It Pa /bin/make
The pdpmake executable.
.It Pa PDPmakefile , makefile , Makefile
Default input makefiles, in search order; strict POSIX mode skips the first.
.It Pa /src/rach2/guest.mk
Kernel makefile.
.It Pa /src/utils/guest.mk
Utility makefile.
.It Pa /src/ish/guest.mk
ISH makefile.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl cd /src/rach2 && make -f guest.mk
.Pp
In the source tree,
.Ql tests/run selfbuild
builds the kernel twice on Rach2 and compares the hashes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr tcc 1
.Sh STANDARDS
.Nm
follows the POSIX.1-2024 Utility Syntax Guidelines, section 12.2, and
implements the make utility with extensions.
All extensions are enabled by default.
Strict POSIX mode can be selected in any of these ways:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Put the special target
.Ql .POSIX
on the first non-comment line of the first input file.
This is the standard method.
.It
Give
.Fl -posix
as the first command-line option.
This method is specific to pdpmake.
.It
Set the environment variable
.Ev PDPMAKE_POSIXLY_CORRECT
to any value.
This method is specific to pdpmake.
.El
.Ss Extensions
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Fl C
changes the working directory.
.It
Double-colon rules are accepted.
.It
The conditional keywords are
.Ql ifdef ,
.Ql ifndef ,
.Ql ifeq ,
.Ql ifneq ,
.Ql else
and
.Ql endif .
.It
Archive members may be written as
.Ql lib.a(mem1.o mem2.o...) .
.It
The macro assignment operator
.Ql :=
is equivalent to the POSIX operator
.Ql ::= .
.It
Inference-rule suffixes may contain any number of periods, including none.
.It
Inference rules may be chained.
Given rules
.Ql .p.q
and
.Ql .q.r
and a file
.Pa thing.p ,
.Nm
can infer how to build
.Pa thing.r .
.It
The wildcards
.Ql * ,
.Ql \&?
and
.Ql []
may occur in targets and prerequisites of target rules.
.It
A
.Ql #
in a command line or macro expansion does not start a comment.
Elsewhere it may be escaped with a backslash.
.It
Expansion of
.Ql $?
removes duplicate prerequisites.
.It
An
.Ql include
line with no files is ignored.
At least one blank must follow
.Ql include .
.It
When errors are not being ignored, the shell that processes build commands
is not started with
.Fl e .
.It
Command-line macro definitions and targets may be mixed;
definitions are processed first.
.It
The internal macros
.Ql $<
and
.Ql $*
have values in target rules.
.It
A target is removed when its build command ends on a signal and errors
are not ignored, unless the target is precious or phony or
.Fl n
or
.Fl p
is in effect.
.It
Inference rules and
.Ql .DEFAULT
are not used for phony targets.
.It
Pragmas propagate to recursive invocations of
.Nm .
.El
.Ss POSIX.1-2024 features
The following apply to POSIX.1-2024 mode:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Macro expansions may be nested, as in
.Ql $(FOO$(BAR)) .
.It
Prerequisites of
.Ql .PHONY
are always considered out of date.
.It
An include line may name more than one file.
.It
.Ql -include file
ignores a missing include file.
.It
Missing or out-of-date include files are rebuilt when a suitable rule exists.
.It
.Ql $^
and
.Ql $+
expand to all prerequisites of the current target, whereas
.Ql $?
lists only those out of date.
.Ql $^
removes duplicates;
.Ql $+
retains them.
.It
If the environment has no
.Ev MAKE
variable, the
.Ql MAKE
macro is initialized from
.Ql argv[0] ,
converting a relative path to an absolute one.
.It
The macro assignment operators
.Ql ::= ,
.Ql :::= ,
.Ql += ,
.Ql ?=
and
.Ql !=
are accepted.
.It
Pattern macros extend suffix substitution to allow prefix changes.
.It
An escaped newline within a macro expansion in a rule becomes a space.
.It
The
.Ql CURDIR
macro is set to the current directory at startup.
.El
